h  school activities but the bigger concern  was staffing shortages use the american  rescue plan funds to incentivize  getting educators to stay in the  profession but also let's consider  bringing back retired teachers cardona  says a long-term solution to get more  teachers in the future was already in  the works at this high school  first time i walked into a classroom of  high school students who are studying to  become teachers  led by a teacher that's getting them  connected to unlv  for now activities like music are  expected to be enhanced by the funding  and help bring a sense of normalcy back  teachers say from the pandemic  extracurriculars is a big thing i hope  you know budgets stay maybe even grow  christian casa is live local now  the money will be dished out once it  actually gets from the federal  government to clark county school  district  state education leaders are trying to  find a way to make it easier to put  substitute teachers in the classroom  some new rules approved this week will  allow those with a high school diploma  to apply for a teaching license all you  need is that high school diploma this  would only apply though during an  emergency declaration which we're in  right now because of the pandemic mary  jane belliesa reports  nevada department of education wants to  make this permanent but there are  concerns about how qualified applicants  are with just a high school diploma and  limited training it's been an ongoing  problem even before the pandemic not  enough teachers and not enough  substitutes kenny belknap with the  commission and educator at liberty high  school says emergency substitute  teachers need more training i find it  troubling especially with these  emergency sub licenses that we're saying  it's okay that you know someone with a  high school equivalent diploma can serve  as a long-term sub someone who can serve  in a classroom with you know 40 plus  kids for an entire school year teaching  them the content area t